	(text_box "MCU, flash, iCE40, and MAX2769 are all connected on the same SPI bus.\n\nTypically iCE40 acts as bus master at startup, reading its configuration from the flash IC. After it is done configuring, MCU assumes the role of bus master, and can then configure MAX2769 or program the flash. In this configuration:\n- iCE40 SPI_SO <-> CIPO\n- iCE40 SPI_SI <-> COPI\n- SPI_SS <-> flash IC nCS w/ pullup. Floats high at startup to select master config. Later iCE40 may drive this line low.\n\nTo program iCE40 via SPI:\n- iCE40 SPI_SO <-> CIPO\n- iCE40 SPI_SI <-> COPI\n- SPI_SS <-> MCU. MCU drives this line low initially."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 368.3 198.9991 0)
		(size 40.64 47.3808)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cb5c0495-b808-4a99-a1f3-1d33f100a284")
	)
